        "correct": 0,
        "explanation": "The work done is equal to the change in kinetic energy: W = ΔK = ½ * 2000 * (20)^2 - 0 = 400,000 J. The time is 5 s, so average power P = W/t = 400,000/5 = 80,000 W. Thus, option A is correct. Option B would be if you used the final velocity squared incorrectly, option C is if you used mass times velocity, and option D is if you forgot to divide by time.",
