        "correct": 0,
        "explanation": "Figure 1 shows that Alzheimer's patients recall 6 words immediately and 2 after delay, a decline of 4 words (a 67% decrease from immediate). Older adults decline from 11 to 8, a decrease of 3 words (27% decrease). Young adults decline from 14 to 12, a 14% decrease. Thus, AD patients show the greatest proportional decline. Option B is false as older adults (8) are lower than young adults (12). Option C is false as AD patients (6) are lower than older adults (11). Option D is contradicted by the differing amounts of decline.",
        "difficulty": "medium",
