        "correct": 0,
        "explanation": "The conclusion that higher MZ concordance reflects genetics assumes that MZ and DZ twins share environments to a similar degree. If parents treat MZ twins more similarly, then greater environmental similarity could explain their higher concordance, weakening the genetic argument. Option B would actually support the twin method because if DZ twins share more environment than siblings, yet show similar concordance, it suggests that extra shared environment does not inflate concordance. Option C is about heritability estimates, not directly about the twin comparison in this study. Option D is irrelevant because sex is not confounded with zygosity in a way that would explain concordance differences.",
