        "question": "The researchers did not perform statistical significance testing between the groups. Which of the following is the most likely consequence of this omission?",
        "options": [
          "The observed differences in concordance rates could be due to chance.",
          "The sample size was too small to detect any real effects.",
          "The concordance rates are invalid because they were not calculated correctly.",
          "The study cannot be used to draw any conclusions about genetic influences."
        ],
        "correct": 0,
        "explanation": "Statistical significance testing assesses the probability that observed differences are due to random variation. Without it, one cannot rule out that the differences between MZ and DZ concordance rates are chance findings. Option B is incorrect because sample size is not the direct consequence of not testing significance; significance tests account for sample size. Option C is incorrect because concordance rates can be calculated accurately without significance testing. Option D is too strong; the study can still provide suggestive evidence, but the lack of significance testing limits confidence in the conclusions.",
